  "question_stem": "{{figure:diagram_q08_01}}\n\nA block $A$ of mass $2\\text{ kg}$ and a particle $B$ of mass $0.5\\text{ kg}$ are connected by a light inextensible string inclined at $15^{\\circ}$ to the horizontal. They are pulled across a horizontal surface with acceleration $1.2\\text{ m s}^{-2}$ by a force of magnitude $6\\text{ N}$, applied to $A$, acting at $20^{\\circ}$ above the horizontal as shown in the diagram. The string and the force applied to $A$ are in the same vertical plane.\n\nThe contact between $B$ and the surface is smooth and the contact between $A$ and the surface is rough.",
